{"name":"Pupil","hex":"#070303","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"pupil","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A learner at a school under the supervision of a teacher.","One who studies under supervision of a renowned expert in their field."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The hole in the middle of the iris of the eye, through which light passes to be focused on the retina.","The central dark part of an ocellated spot."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pupil"}],"entries":[{"title":"Pupil","blocks":[{"text":"The pupil is a hole located in the center of the iris of the eye that allows light to strike the retina. It appears black because light rays entering the pupil are either absorbed by the tissues inside the eye directly, or absorbed after diffuse reflections within the eye that mostly miss exiting the narrow pupil. The size of the pupil is controlled by the iris, and varies depending on many factors, the most significant being the amount of light in the environment. The term \"pupil\" was coined by Gerard of Cremona."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/65/Eye_iris.jpg/330px-Eye_iris.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pupil","wikidata":"Q173318"},{"title":"Pupil (band)","blocks":[{"text":"Pupil are a Filipino alternative rock band. They currently consist of vocalist Ely Buendia, lead guitarist Jerome Velasco, bassist Dok Sergio, and drummer Wendell Garcia."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pupil_(band)","wikidata":"Q7260659"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dc/Pupillary_light_reflex.jpg/500px-Pupillary_light_reflex.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dc/Pupillary_light_reflex.jpg/1280px-Pupillary_light_reflex.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dc/Pupillary_light_reflex.jpg/500px-Pupillary_light_reflex.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The pupil diameter can vary greatly due to various factors (primarily the pupillary light reflex), from constriction to as small as 2 mm, to dilation larger than 8 mm in some individuals, though the maximal dilation also varies substantially by individual and decreases with age","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APupillary_light_reflex.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b7/Voluntary_pupil_dilation.gif/500px-Voluntary_pupil_dilation.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b7/Voluntary_pupil_dilation.gif/500px-Voluntary_pupil_dilation.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A human adult exhibiting voluntary control over his iris muscles, which grants him the ability to dilate and constrict his pupils on command","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AVoluntary_pupil_dilation.gif"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/19/Human_eye_in_dim_light.jpg/500px-Human_eye_in_dim_light.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/19/Human_eye_in_dim_light.jpg/1280px-Human_eye_in_dim_light.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/19/Human_eye_in_dim_light.jpg/500px-Human_eye_in_dim_light.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Pupil dilated naturally to 9 mm due to dim light. The subject is an extreme case, as most individuals are not able to naturally dilate their pupils to that extent","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHuman_eye_in_dim_light.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bc/Human_eye_in_bright_light.jpg/500px-Human_eye_in_bright_light.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bc/Human_eye_in_bright_light.jpg/500px-Human_eye_in_bright_light.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Pupil constriction can be in response to negative emotional states","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHuman_eye_in_bright_light.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d3/Horizontal_Rectangular_Pupil_of_a_Goat.jpg/120px-Horizontal_Rectangular_Pupil_of_a_Goat.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d3/Horizontal_Rectangular_Pupil_of_a_Goat.jpg/250px-Horizontal_Rectangular_Pupil_of_a_Goat.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d3/Horizontal_Rectangular_Pupil_of_a_Goat.jpg/120px-Horizontal_Rectangular_Pupil_of_a_Goat.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHorizontal_Rectangular_Pupil_of_a_Goat.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fc/Taeniura_grabata_eye.jpg/250px-Taeniura_grabata_eye.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fc/Taeniura_grabata_eye.jpg/500px-Taeniura_grabata_eye.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fc/Taeniura_grabata_eye.jpg/250px-Taeniura_grabata_eye.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w